  "body": "Slice 2 of #926. Slice 1 was PR #1002 (the recorded edge-case streams and the per-`.cps` script suites). This PR moves the ten app suites named in the issue to `crates/post/tests`. They used app only to generate a toolpath before posting it; now they read recorded input instead.\n\n## What changed\n- **Moved to `crates/post/tests`:** `fanuc_post`, `probe_dialects`, `probe_guard`, `probe_report`, `probe_tormach`, `inverted_probe`, `arc_planes`, `inverted_equivalence`, `inverted_post`, and the posting half of `vertical_arc_entry`. Their helpers `inverted_support/` and `macro_b/` moved with them.\n- **Recorded inputs (`crates/post/tests/recorded/inputs/`):**\n  - 28 probe `.cnc` streams, one per distinct (cycle, dump) pair the old tests built.\n  - 5 probe paths as `.cl`. `cl::text` carries no touches, so `probe_guard`'s \"every GUARD is a positioning feed of the path\" law needs the path and the stream side by side.\n  - 3 contour `.cl` paths for `vertical_arc_entry`.\n  - The inverted-axis fixture stream.\n- **Generator-side guards.** Each one compares byte for byte and rewrites the file with `WRITE_GOLDEN=1`:\n  - App's `recorded_post_streams` (slice 1's guard suite) guards the probe streams and paths, generated by `motion::probing::probe_cycle` and `post::dump`. App is still the only crate that sees both motion and post. Its new `every_recorded_input_has_a_generator` fails on any file in `inputs/` that nothing writes.\n  - `crates/motion/tests/vertical_arc_entry.rs` is the generator half: true arcs, tangency, the oblique note and verify. It also guards the three contour recordings.\n  - Post's `inverted_post` guards `inverted_probe.cnc`. App's `inverted_axis_display` reads that file, so app no longer carries a copy of `inverted_support`.\n- **Stays in app:** the `ArcDto` project-file test, now in `float_roundtrip`, as the #919 research said.\n- **Goldens:** they stay in `crates/app/tests/golden/` (the post suites use `recorded::app_golden`), because other app suites and xtask read them. **No golden changed.** One home for the goldens is #919's sub-issue 6.\n- **xtask:** the asset and gate-map unit tests named `fanuc_post` / `arc_planes` as app suites. They now read every crate's `<crate> suites` step. **PROCESS_VERSION 33.** A fork pulls the process files as usual; nothing else is needed.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/926-recorded-app-post-tests.md`.\n\n## Done means\n- **The 10 tests run outside app from recorded input:** yes. The one `ArcDto` test stays in app by design (it tests the project file).\n- **No new dependency between crates:** none. No `Cargo.toml` changed.\n- **Each recorded file has a generator-side test that fails when it goes stale:** yes. I checked this by appending a line to a recording (`every_recorded_probe_stream_is_current` failed and named the file) and by adding an orphan file (`every_recorded_input_has_a_generator` failed).\n\n## Test counts\n- Before: 79 `#[test]`s in the ten files.\n- After: those 79 still run; 78 are in post and the `ArcDto` test is in app `float_roundtrip`. Post gains 1 new guard.\n- New guard tests: post `inverted_post::the_recorded_inverted_probe_stream_is_current`; app `every_recorded_probe_stream_is_current`, `every_recorded_probe_path_is_current` and `every_recorded_input_has_a_generator`.\n- Motion `vertical_arc_entry` holds 3 generator-half tests, under the same names as the originals.\n- Golden asserts are unchanged.\n\n## How tested\n- The quick gate passes on head 9338316c (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): post suites (all 29), motion `vertical_arc_entry` (3 fns), app `float_roundtrip` / `inverted_axis_display` / `recorded_post_streams`, and the xtask unit tests (76).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings` is clean. It compiles every app test, which confirms no app suite still uses the moved helpers.\n\n## Not exercised\n- Batch and release tiers.\n- `fanuc_post`'s \"hair under zero\" probe case was posted from a serialized stream before this PR as well, so its recording is byte-identical to the zero-edge one (the stream is in microns). I kept it as its own file and noted this in the test.\n\n## Overlap\n- PR #1034 (#995, a probe section starts no coolant) touches probe posting. If it changes a probe stream or golden, whichever PR merges second regenerates with `WRITE_GOLDEN=1`.\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0; branch carries upstream/main merged (process files at upstream's PROCESS_VERSION before this bump).\n\nChangelog: none (test-only move)\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #926\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n\n",
